\frac{8}{5}=-\\frac{5}{5}+\\frac{8}{5}=\\frac{-5+8}{5}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $8$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $8$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/0b/0b6274b1cb65e330c81602212fe081835eb86c1c1c8e3a6eee278fbfd2614776.png)\n\nSo, $-5+8=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-5+8}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-5+8}{5}=\\frac{8-5}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-1+\\frac{8}{5}=\\frac{3}{5}.$"}]}
